<Layout title="About"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CONTEXT</p><h1>A researcher.<br/>And a person, too.</h1></header><div class="about-layout"><div class="prose"><p>I’m Haoran Qian <span lang="zh-CN">（钱皓冉）</span>, studying Computer Science at Huazhong University of Science and Technology.</p><p>My interests are broad by design: world models, generative models, video generation, multimodal learning, and embodied intelligence. I am drawn to problems that connect representation, generation, and an understanding of how worlds change.</p><h2>Outside research</h2><p>I enjoy writing, photography, wandering around unfamiliar cities, and occasionally turning memories into stories.</p><p>This website keeps both kinds of attention in one place: things I am trying to understand, and things I do not want to forget.</p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></div><aside class="currently"><h2>Currently</h2><dl><dt><span aria-hidden="true">📖</span> READING</dt><dd>Papers on world models and video generation.</dd><dt><span aria-hidden="true">💭</span> THINKING</dt><dd>How models represent change over time.</dd><dt><span aria-hidden="true">🧪</span> LEARNING</dt><dd>Generative video and multimodal systems.</dd><dt><span aria-hidden="true">📍</span> ELSEWHERE</dt><dd><a href={site.github}>GitHub ↗</a><br/><a href="/fragments/">Fragments / 浮光 ↗</a></dd></dl></aside></div></Layout>
